# Project-management docs

This rule auto-attaches when editing repo-level management material. This is the
**project tier** — it governs how the repo evolves, not any single node.

- Keep node-specific implementation detail **out** of these files; link to the node instead.
- `docs/roadmap.md` tracks planned / in-progress / done items.
- `docs/decisions/` holds ADRs. Add a new numbered ADR (`NNNN-title.md`) for any
  significant structural or directional decision; never rewrite history in an
  accepted ADR — supersede it with a new one.
- `CHANGELOG.md` is a human-readable, repo-wide log. Add an entry when a node is
  added/removed or when project-level structure changes.
- When a decision changes conventions, update `docs/conventions.md` and reference the ADR.
